      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following number lines represents the inequality $-3<x<1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The inequality $-3<x<1$ means that $x$ can take any value greater than $-3,$ and less than $1.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we draw an open circle at $-3$ and another open circle at $1.$ Then, we highlight the region between the points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14168182/assets/f6139cea308db19681b8e2239e01f77d4af406a728041aa738b29ee3ce6a603e.png)",
