    "q-54820": {
      "dom_id": "step-q54820",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14168182/assets/f2fc2248ce56cd8209d9f6438d24c7f9e9f805f320ef5549be25282cfbaa6e61.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?",
      "worked_solution": "The red rays contain all values less than  $-1$ or greater than $1.$ In addition,\n\n- the open circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $-1,$ and\n\n- the open circle at $1$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $1.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<-1$ or $x>1.$",
